      "id": 2,
      "text": "British and American planters established rice plantations along the Black River near Dunbar starting in the 1730s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/dunbar_south_carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "After the Civil War, several freedmen collectively acquired the Dunbar Plantation to establish an independent rural community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/dunbar_georgetown_county_south_carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Black River near Dunbar features dense swamp forests with ancient bald cypress trees that color the water a dark tea-like hue.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
